  "behavior": [
    "Neighbors use the original selected set. Additive steps retain seeds without cascading.",
    "Periodic controls and analytic circle controls wrap; closed clamped NURBS controls stop at their boundaries.",
    "Edit grips have no logical neighbors: shifts clear their picks, additive and row commands retain them. Mesh grips are excluded and retained.",
    "Preselected EditPtOn owners stay selected. Closed edit-point seams use one displayed grip and retain both interpolation endpoint constraints.",
    "Layouts are computed once per affected owner. Row unions scan each affected net once."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "SelUV uses a separate interactive surface-row picker; see select-uv-rows-validation.json for its subsequent implementation.",
    "This native corpus uses public API grip setup and completed direct command macros. Arbitrary native mouse input and nested getter parity are not qualified.",
    "SubD/solid grips, per-grip hiding, all composite arrangements and extreme/non-clamped layouts remain unqualified.",
    "Closed edit-seam transforms have independent equation regressions; native edited-geometry parity is not added by this selection corpus.",
    "No new edited-file roundtrip or performance parity claim. Oracle timings include harness and document overhead."
  ]
